                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There's really nothing else like Google Earth VR. If I could go into the past and show a medieval era person any one thing from the modern day, it wouldn't be a smart phone, it would be a VR headset with this loaded up. Not only because the experience of seeing the Earth from God's point of view is enough to bring a tear to your eye, but because of what was required to build it. The satellites that had to be put in space, the lidar drones that had be flown around, the google earth vans that had to self drive all over the earth, all the math and software that went into indexing all that data, fetching it on demand and rendering it in stereoscopic 3D and 360 degree images. All this to enable you to go and see any place on the entire earth. To see any city and go see their architecture, to see their language, to see their mountains and their lakes, to see their high rises and slums and parks and stadiums and trash and animals and cars, all of it. The whole world in your hands to explore whenever you want, completely free, just for the love of the Earth we all share. When I imagine the kinds of things that God envisioned human creating as they matured, I think of Google Earth VR.",
